<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime entitlements for the Developer ID build (BTL-258). electron-builder.yml uses this file for both the
  app (mac.entitlements) and everything signed inside it (mac.entitlementsInherit): the Electron helpers, the frameworks,
  node-pty's pty.node and spawn-helper, and the shipherd-hook binary. Only the Developer ID build uses it; the ad-hoc build
  (no signing secrets) is signed without the hardened runtime by scripts/after-pack.cjs, so these do not apply there.

  Deliberately left out:
  - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: every library Shipherd loads (Electron's frameworks, node-pty's
    pty.node) is inside the bundle and re-signed with the same Team ID, so library validation passes. The memory MCP
    servers (ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE) are plain JavaScript with no native addons.
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables, com.apple.security.cs.debugger: nothing needs them.
  - com.apple.security.automation.apple-events, device.camera / device.audio-input: Shipherd sends no Apple Events and
    uses no camera or microphone. Child processes (claude, git, gh, the user's shell) are separate programs with their
    own signatures; the hardened runtime does not limit what Shipherd may spawn.
  If a change needs one of these, add it here with the reason and say so in the PR.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!--
      V8 generates machine code at run time and needs MAP_JIT pages. Without this the main process, the renderer
      helper, the memory MCP servers (the Shipherd binary run with ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE) and shipherd-hook (a Node SEA
      binary) crash at start-up under the hardened runtime.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      Node and V8 still write some executable memory without MAP_JIT (Node's own macOS release builds carry this
      entitlement for the same reason). It covers the Node side of Shipherd: shipherd-hook and the ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE
      memory MCP servers.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
